phs. J. Comb. Theory A. 1986.\n- Galvin, David. Three tutorial lectures on entropy and counting. 2014-06-30.\n\n## Combinatorial version\n\nLet \\mathcal{F} be a family of subsets of [n] (possibly with repeats) with each i\\in [n] included in at least t members of \\mathcal{F}. Let \\mathcal{A} be another set of subsets of [n]. Then\n\n  \\mathcal |\\mathcal{A}|\\leq \\prod_{F\\in \\mathcal{F}}|\\operatorname{trace}_{F}(\\mathcal{A})|^{1/t}\n\nwhere  \\operatorname{trace}_{F}(\\mathcal{A})=\\{A\\cap F:A\\in\\mathcal{A}\\} the set of possible intersections of elements of  \\mathcal{A} with  F.\n\n## See also\n\n* Lovász local lemma\n\n## References\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n40  Common Information and Matroid Representation (https://crises-deim.urv.cat/web/docs/publications/theses/mBamiloshin.pdf)\nciteturn2search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; Crawled: 5.1 years ago; 40  Common Information and Matroid Representation ... ** In this proof we employ the conditional mutual information and conditional entropy where we use the submodularity and monotonicity properties of the Shannon entropy. ... = r(B)+3r(AC)+r(AD)-2r(A)-r(C)-r(BC)-r(CD)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[Literature Review] Counting q-Matroids (https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/counting-q-matroids)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; The paper \"Counting $q$-matroids\" by Jany, Jurrius, and Pendavingh addresses the enumeration of $q$-matroids, a $q$-analogue of classical matroids, defined over a fixed ground space $E \\cong \\mathbb{F}_q^n$ with a prescribed rank $r$. ... Entropy-Based Method (for $\\mathcal{M}_q$): Utilizing Shearer’s Product Theorem, the authors establish an entropy-counting argument applicable to classes closed under contraction. ... The authors analyze the growth in three regimes: $n \\to \\infty$ (fixed $r$), $n=2r$ with $r \\to \\infty$